  "body": "From webkit/LayoutTests/transforms/cssmatrix-3d-interface.xhtml:\n\n```\ndebug(\"Test throwing exception from inverse\");\nm = new WebKitCSSMatrix(\"matrix(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)\"); // not invertible\nshouldThrow('m.inverse()');\n```\n\nCurrently `inverse` is defined in terms of `DOMMatrix.invertSelf` which says to do: \"If the current matrix is not invertible set all attributes to NaN and set is2D to false. \"\n\nBut Chrome, Safari and edge throw `DOMException` `NotSupportedError`s\n",
